; WHO 13 gateway identification: the requests a client sends to learn which
; gateway it talks to, in the order MyHOME's runtime uses them (MyHOME#420).
;
; Grammar (Encyclopedia functional/who-13-integration-gateway/dimensions.md,
; functional/who-1013-diagnostics):
;   *#13**15##    DIMENSION 15  device type (official code; 200 is shared by the
;                               F454 / F461 / MyHomeServer1 / MH202 class)
;   *#13**16##    DIMENSION 16  firmware version
;   *#13**12##    DIMENSION 12  MAC address
;   *#13**10##    DIMENSION 10  IP address
;   *#13**11##    DIMENSION 11  netmask
;   *#13**23##    DIMENSION 23  kernel version
;   *#13**24##    DIMENSION 24  distribution version
;   *#1013**1##   WHO 1013 OBJECT_MODEL (134 = F461, 19 = H4684, 4 = MH200)
;   *#1013*0*1##  the same with WHERE 0
;
; DIMENSION 19 (uptime) and 27 (host name) are left out: their values depend on
; the run, not on the firmware.
;
; Question: which of these does each firmware answer, and does any of them
; harm the gateway? A client that adds a gateway by hand (no SSDP) has only
; these frames to find out what it is talking to. Every step runs on a
; freshly started gateway (reset=each).
down *#13**15##
down *#13**16##
down *#13**12##
down *#13**10##
down *#13**11##
down *#13**23##
down *#13**24##
down *#1013**1##
down *#1013*0*1##
